#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Replace PUB tuples with a `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Étape 3. Remplacer les tuples PUB par un `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of passing a list of tuples (PUBs), when using Executor, you build a `QuantumProgram` and append _items_ to it.\n"
msgstr "Au lieu de passer une liste de tuples (PUB), lorsque tu utilises Executor, tu construis un `QuantumProgram` et tu y ajoutes des _éléments_.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `QuantumProgram` accepts _circuit_ items and _samplex_ items:\n"
msgstr "Un `QuantumProgram` accepte des éléments de type _circuit_ et _samplex_ :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Appends a `CircuitItem`, which is a circuit and (optionally) its\n"
"parameter values. It is executed as-is, without any randomization. \n"
msgstr ""
"`append_circuit_item` : Ajoute un `CircuitItem`, qui est un circuit et (facultativement) ses\n"
"valeurs de paramètres. Il est exécuté tel quel, sans aucune randomisation. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this when you just want to sample a circuit, exactly as Sampler would with a PUB that has no\n"
"  twirling; for example, when submitting a plain sampling job, or when you already manually included any\n"
"  variants you want.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Appends a `samplexItem`, which is a *template circuit* plus a\n"
"  *samplex* that generates randomized parameter sets on the server side. \n"
msgstr ""
"  Utilise ceci lorsque tu veux simplement échantillonner un circuit, exactement comme le ferait Sampler avec un PUB sans\n"
"  twirling ; par exemple, lors de la soumission d'un job d'échantillonnage simple, ou lorsque tu as déjà inclus manuellement les\n"
"  variantes que tu souhaites.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item` : Ajoute un `samplexItem`, qui est un *circuit modèle* plus un\n"
"  *samplex* qui génère des ensembles de paramètres randomisés côté serveur. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this\n"
"  when you want the circuit's content randomized. The primary case is with \n"
"  twirling (gate or measurement) or noise injection. This capability replaces\n"
"  Sampler's built-in twirling.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Utilise ceci\n"
"  lorsque tu veux que le contenu du circuit soit randomisé. Le cas principal est avec le\n"
"  twirling (de porte ou de mesure) ou l'injection de bruit. Cette capacité remplace\n"
"  le twirling intégré de Sampler.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single `QuantumProgram` can accept both item types; each appended item is executed as an\n"
"independent task and produces its own entry in the results. In general, use `append_circuit_item` when your circuit does not need to be randomized. Otherwise, use `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un seul `QuantumProgram` peut accepter les deux types d'éléments ; chaque élément ajouté est exécuté comme une\n"
"tâche indépendante et produit sa propre entrée dans les résultats. En général, utilise `append_circuit_item` lorsque ton circuit n'a pas besoin d'être randomisé. Sinon, utilise `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next sections show each in turn: parameterized circuits that use \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, and migrating twirling by using `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les sections suivantes montrent chacune à tour de rôle : les circuits paramétrés qui utilisent \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, et la migration du twirling en utilisant `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following code examples, `isa_circuit` refers to the circuit that has been transpiled to conform to the target backend's [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA). This `isa_circuit` contains two parameters.\n"
msgstr "Dans les exemples de code suivants, `isa_circuit` fait référence au circuit qui a été transpilé pour se conformer à l'[architecture du jeu d'instructions](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA) du backend cible. Ce `isa_circuit` contient deux paramètres.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"param-circuits\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3a. Migrate parameterized circuits {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"
msgstr "Étape 3a. Migrer les circuits paramétrés {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Sampler, parameter values are the second element of the PUB tuple. With Executor,\n"
"pass them as `circuit_arguments` to `append_circuit_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Avec Sampler, les valeurs des paramètres sont le deuxième élément du tuple PUB. Avec Executor,\n"
"passe-les en tant que `circuit_arguments` à `append_circuit_item`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor**\n"
msgstr "**Executor**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3b. Migrate built-in twirling to explicit annotations {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"
msgstr "Étape 3b. Migrer le twirling intégré vers des annotations explicites {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the most significant change. Sampler applies twirling for you by using options. With \n"
"Executor, you declare that intent explicitly by using annotated boxes and\n"
"a samplex (from [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"
msgstr ""
"C'est le changement le plus important. Sampler applique le twirling à ta place en utilisant des options. Avec \n"
"Executor, tu déclares cette intention explicitement en utilisant des boîtes annotées et\n"
"un samplex (depuis [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler (twirling by using options):**\n"
msgstr "**Sampler (twirling en utilisant des options) :**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor (twirling by using boxes and a samplex):**\n"
msgstr "**Executor (twirling en utilisant des boîtes et un samplex) :**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the template circuit and samplex are built on the client side, you can\n"
"inspect and sample them locally to verify the output before sending anything to\n"
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme le circuit modèle et le samplex sont construits côté client, tu peux\n"
"les inspecter et les échantillonner localement pour vérifier la sortie avant d'envoyer quoi que ce soit au\n"
"matériel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-local\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification: Sample the template circuit locally {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"
msgstr "Vérification : Échantillonner le circuit modèle localement {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can draw randomizations from the samplex and bind them to the template\n"
"circuit to confirm that the samplex is producing the parameter values you expect.\n"
"The parameter values returned by `samplex.sample` are directly compatible with the\n"
"template circuit's parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tu peux tirer des randomisations du samplex et les lier au circuit\n"
"modèle pour confirmer que le samplex produit les valeurs de paramètres attendues.\n"
"Les valeurs de paramètres renvoyées par `samplex.sample` sont directement compatibles avec les\n"
"paramètres du circuit modèle.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To go further, you can verify that each randomization is logically equivalent to the\n"
"original circuit by, for example, converting both to `Operator` objects and comparing their unitary implementations (after\n"
"accounting for the `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` corrections that undo\n"
"measurement twirling), or by comparing expectation values from a local\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` or `StatevectorEstimator` run. See the Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"guide for a complete walkthrough.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour aller plus loin, tu peux vérifier que chaque randomisation est logiquement équivalente au\n"
"circuit d'origine en, par exemple, convertissant les deux en objets `Operator` et en comparant leurs implémentations unitaires (après\n"
"avoir pris en compte les corrections `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` qui annulent\n"
"le twirling de mesure), ou en comparant des valeurs d'espérance issues d'une exécution locale de\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` ou `StatevectorEstimator`. Consulte le guide Samplomatic\n"
"[Entrées et sorties du samplex](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"pour un tutoriel complet.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shots\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Change how shots are requested {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"
msgstr "Étape 4. Changer comment les shots sont demandés {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move shots from the PUB to `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  In Executor, `shots` applies to the whole job. Submit multiple jobs if you need different shot counts.\n"
msgstr "Déplace les shots du PUB vers `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  Dans Executor, `shots` s'applique à l'ensemble du job. Soumets plusieurs jobs si tu as besoin de nombres de shots différents.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"options\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5. Update options as necessary {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"
msgstr "Étape 5. Mettre à jour les options si nécessaire {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are fewer options available to Executor than Sampler, because\n"
"error-mitigation choices now live in your annotations and samplex instead of options.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il y a moins d'options disponibles pour Executor que pour Sampler, car\n"
"les choix d'atténuation d'erreurs résident maintenant dans tes annotations et ton samplex plutôt que dans les options.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also a structural difference in where settings live. \n"
msgstr "Il existe aussi une différence structurelle dans l'emplacement des paramètres. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Sampler,\n"
"everything, including choices that affect result post-processing, is configured on\n"
"the primitive's options or in the PUB. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Avec Sampler,\n"
"tout, y compris les choix qui affectent le post-traitement des résultats, est configuré dans\n"
"les options de la primitive ou dans le PUB. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Executor, choices that affect how the job\n"
"results are shaped and post-processed are set on the [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), not on\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Avec Executor, les choix qui influent sur la manière dont les résultats\n"
"du job sont structurés et post-traités sont définis sur le [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), et non sur\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples:\n"
msgstr "Examples:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) holds only lower-level execution and environment\n"
"settings that don't change the structure of the returned data. It has three top-level groups:\n"
msgstr "[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) ne contient que des paramètres d'exécution et d'environnement de plus bas niveau qui ne modifient pas la structure des données renvoyées. Il comporte trois groupes de premier niveau :\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"
msgstr "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Contains fewer options than with Sampler.  For example, there  is no `meas_type` Executor option. \n"
msgstr "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)) : contient moins d'options qu'avec Sampler. Par exemple, il n'y a pas d'option Executor `meas_type`. \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"
msgstr "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notably, the `twirling` and `dynamical_decoupling` options exist in Sampler but not Executor. Instead, those option values are expressed through the directed execution model.\n"
msgstr "Notamment, les options `twirling` et `dynamical_decoupling` existent dans Sampler mais pas dans Executor. À la place, les valeurs de ces options sont exprimées via le modèle d'exécution dirigée.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example:**\n"
msgstr "**Example:**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-job\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 6. Update the `run` command {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"
msgstr "Étape 6. Mettre à jour la commande `run` {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The input to an Executor job is the program, instead of PUBs.\n"
msgstr "L'entrée d'un job Executor est le programme, au lieu de PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 7. Change how you access results {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"
msgstr "Étape 7. Modifier la façon dont tu accèdes aux résultats {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Executor, results are NumPy arrays, not `BitArray` objects.  Use the name string as the index (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) and get an `np.ndarray` back. There is no need to remember the `.data.<register>` attribute path.\n"
msgstr "Dans Executor, les résultats sont des tableaux NumPy, et non des objets `BitArray`. Utilise la chaîne de nom comme index (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) pour obtenir un `np.ndarray` en retour. Il n'est pas nécessaire de se souvenir du chemin d'attribut `.data.<register>`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To update from Sampler to Executor, change `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` to `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, then rewrite `get_counts`-based post-processing as NumPy operations.\n"
msgstr "Pour passer de Sampler à Executor, remplace `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` par `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, puis réécris le post-traitement basé sur `get_counts` sous forme d'opérations NumPy.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sampler's `BitArray` offers helpers (`get_counts`, `slice_bits`, `slice_shots`, `expectation_values`, and post-selection masks). Executor returns raw NumPy arrays so you can perform this post-processing with standard NumPy operations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirled-results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 8. Handle twirled results (bit-flip corrections) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"
msgstr "Étape 8. Gérer les résultats twirlés (corrections de bit-flip) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you apply measurement twirling through a `SamplexItem`, Executor returns the raw\n"
"(twirled) measurements plus the bit-flip corrections needed to undo the twirling.\n"
"You need to apply them manually; nothing is corrected implicitly. \n"
msgstr ""
"Lorsque tu appliques un twirling de mesure via un `SamplexItem`, Executor renvoie les mesures brutes\n"
"(twirlées) ainsi que les corrections de bit-flip nécessaires pour annuler le twirling.\n"
"Tu dois les appliquer manuellement ; rien n'est corrigé implicitement. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using Executor, undo twirling explicitly by using the `measurement_flips.<reg>` corrections and an XOR, as shown in the following example:\n"
msgstr "Lorsque tu utilises Executor, annule le twirling explicitement en utilisant les corrections `measurement_flips.<reg>` et un XOR, comme le montre l'exemple suivant :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no equivalent step in Sampler because it undoes twirling for you.\n"
msgstr "Il n'y a pas d'étape équivalente dans Sampler, car il annule le twirling pour toi.\n"

